  "background": [
    {
      "text": "All FCU controls are inoperative. A/THR, AP 1 + 2 and FD 1 + 2 are not available (except in LAND or GO AROUND mode, where only A/THR is lost).",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-AUTO_FLT",
          "page": "P 22/42",
          "pdf": 2999
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the PFD: altitude alert inoperative; ILS/GLS/MLS deviation scales displayed; flight path vector displayed; Mach indication inoperative; FMA lost except in LAND or GA mode.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-AUTO_FLT",
          "page": "P 22/42",
          "pdf": 2999
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the ND: ARC mode with map (20 NM range) is displayed. Needle 1 is related to VOR1 only; needle 2 to ADF 2 only. The weather radar image may be lost; if it remains displayed it must be disregarded. In all cases the WXR RNG message is displayed.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-AUTO_FLT",
          "page": "P 22/42",
          "pdf": 2999
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An A/THR disconnection caused by a failure is a non-standard disconnection: the engines hold the thrust set before it, THR LK flashes on the FMA and ENG THRUST LOCKED appears every 5 s. The lock ends as soon as the thrust levers are moved.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-22_30-50-40",
          "page": "P 2/4",
          "pdf": 1193
        },
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-ENG",
          "page": "P 224/226",
          "pdf": 3471
        },
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-22_30-80-20",
          "page": "P 34/36",
          "pdf": 1259
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alpha-floor protection is inhibited when both FCU channels are failed.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-22_40-30",
          "page": "P 4/4",
          "pdf": 1279
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "technique": [
    {
      "text": "STOP ECAM before reading STATUS to consider system resets, from the QRH reset table only. Baro setting is one of the actions that needs both pilots.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "AOP-30-30",
          "page": "P 3/6",
          "pdf": 84
        },
