  "gaps": [
    {
      "text": "The FCTM has no technique for this failure (PR-AEP-AUTOFLT covers FMGC failure only), and the PDP has no module for it. Fly/thrust items come from the FCOM layer 2 text and the DSC thrust-lock description.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-AUTOFLT",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 394
        },
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-22_30-50-40",
          "page": "P 2/4",
          "pdf": 1193
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCOM names no pilot for changing the standby altimeter; the brief shows the PM, confirmed by the user. It names no pilot for not inserting the MDA (MDH), shown for both pilots. It names the PM only for the callouts.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-AUTO_FLT",
          "page": "P 22/42",
          "pdf": 2999
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCOM says the FMA is lost except in LAND or GA mode, and also that THR LK flashes on the FMA. The manuals do not reconcile the two. The brief only states the conflict, confirmed by the user.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "PRO-ABN-AUTO_FLT",
          "page": "P 22/42",
          "pdf": 2999
        },
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-22_30-50-40",
          "page": "P 2/4",
          "pdf": 1193
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "HS-TO-only QRH version of the reset (02.15A) is excluded.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "QRH",
          "code": "02.15",
          "page": "02.15A",
          "pdf": 73
        }
      ]
    }
